  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 233 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nNumerous waves of theta-e advection will occur into Friday with \nprecipitation chances increasing further east into central Iowa as \nLee side cyclogenesis occurs over eastern Colorado to Wyoming. The \ncyclogenesis will push additional moisture into Iowa and bring more \nwidespread potential for showers and a few non-severe thunderstorms. \nPWAT values Friday night and Saturday will be over 1.5 inches over \nIowa along with 850 mb dew points near 12C and warm cloud depths \nnear 13 kft. These parameters will be favorable for warm rain \nprocesses and a efficient rain producing system. Deep convection \nwill be lacking, which in this case, maximum rainfall rates are not \nexpected. The deep layer moisture will diminish on Sunday but \nstratus may linger over parts of Iowa into early next week. A potent \nupper level system remains on track to impact Iowa Tuesday and \nTuesday night. Locally heavy rainfall and perhaps a few strong \nstorms will be possible.",
